# Fluent Mobile agent instructions (Cursor)

**Canonical source:** `CLAUDE.md` — stack, layout, conventions, PR workflow, and
agent scoping. Always-on Cursor rules in `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` remain the
injected contract; do not duplicate them here.

**Reuse (do not duplicate):**

- Skills: `.claude/skills/*/SKILL.md`
- Commands / workflows: `.claude/commands/*.md`
- Review agents: `.claude/agents/*.md`
- PR template: `.cursor/templates/pr-template.md` (use with
  `/generate-pr-description` or `/create-pr`; GitHub UI mirror
  `.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md`) — **one format only**

**Agent models:** repo agents under `.claude/agents/` use `model: inherit` so
Cursor Auto / the session model apply (do not pin model aliases). The PR
delivery gate still requires running `code-reviewer` before handoff.

When a task matches a skill description, read that `SKILL.md` first. To run a
command, read and follow `.claude/commands/<name>.md` directly — every command
works this way in Cursor and any other agent tool, not only Claude Code.

**Discovery contract:** the globs above are the contract — any skill, command,
or agent added under `.claude/` is automatically in scope for Cursor and other
agent tools, with no per-item registration step.

**Repo workflow:** PRs target `main`. Track work in **GitHub Issues** on
Project 4 (`Refs #NNN` in the PR body — never closing keywords). See
`docs/issue-tracking.md`.

**Global IDE user rules:** if they conflict with this repo, prefer `CLAUDE.md`,
`.cursor/rules/`, and this file.

**Cursor-only:** session env + architecture-guard hooks in `.cursor/hooks.json`
(warn-only; never deny tools).

**Cursor command shims (optional):** a `.cursor/commands/*.md` file only makes a
command appear in Cursor's `/` palette — it is **not** required for the command
to work (read the canonical `.claude/commands/<name>.md` directly per the
discovery contract above). When a shim exists it points at
`.claude/commands/*.md`; edit the `.claude` file as the single source of truth
and never duplicate logic into the shim.
